Z||000000||topcat||12-30-2001||12:34 PM||||Good afternoon all.  I read somewhere that the Firebird (84-86) headlight motors were the same as the Fiero, but the sides are opposite, so if you wanted a right side motor for your Fiero, get a left one from a Firebird.  Can anyone tell me if this is fact or fiction.  I thought I read somewhere else that the motors had the same gears, so if you wanted to use one from a firebird, you would have to take just the gear out of it.  I am in need aof a motor, gears on mine are severely stripped out.  None of the junkyards around here have any Fiero motors, but there are a lot of Firebird motors.  Will the whole motor work, or will I have to take the gear out of it?  If I can only use the gear, I will order one from the internet, but If I can use the whole motor, I will.<P>Advice please<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||12-30-2001||01:29 PM||||If the gears are shot, go to the FIERO PARTS VENDORS (top of screen)and look up Rodney Dickman.  For about $4.00 he has a kit to fix the problem.  I don't know about the Firebird motors.||||reg||3
Z||000002||mbramble||12-30-2001||01:38 PM||||Check out the info here:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/headlight.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/headlight.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||topcat||12-30-2001||01:50 PM||||Thanks, this link is for the site where I first read about the interchangability.  The article says that "The Firebird motors appear to be entirely interchangeable with the Fiero motors..."  It does not give a difinitive answer, ergo the question.  Does anyone have first hand knowledge?   In regards to buying one for less than $5.00, Where can I get it?  Rodney's costs $21.00 for a kit to repair one light motor.  If I can not find one locally, I will get the brass ones from the guy that sells them in Florida. ||||reg||14
Z||000004||Rodney||12-30-2001||01:52 PM||||87-92 Firebird motors are the same as the 84-86 Fiero. Same GM part number. But they are switched. Firebird pass. side is the Fiero drivers side etc. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||topcat||12-30-2001||01:55 PM||||Thanks Rodney, one of the local yards here is going to give me the motors for 25.00 out of a wrecked Firebird. I think I am going to stock up on them...  He has a couple of "Birds" in his yard.<P>||||reg||7
Z||000006||Bill Shenefelt||01-01-2002||07:26 AM||||Oops, if the 87+ firebird motors match the PRE 87 Fiero motors, does the relay for the 87+ firebird really match the 87+ fiero?  If so,what does it take to use "old Fiero relays" on a New 87+ fiero motor? <BR>ps: Rodney, I like the short shifter you sent, re my phone call to you last week.<P>------------------<BR>Bill Shenefelt||||reg||1
